cmtnajsui004733ituo2pcouq	Experience: I didn’t know I was pregnant until I gave birth	There’d been no morning sickness, cravings or tiredness. My mum didn’t believe I’d had a baby – even after seeing her on FaceTime\nWhen I was 19, I went to college in Texas, where I met my ­boyfriend Preston. It was 2023 and I had big plans. After ­finishing my degree in criminal justice, I wanted to go to law school. I wasn’t in a rush to get married or have kids. My mum had drilled into me a fear of getting pregnant at a young age. I was on the pill and careful with contraception.\nIn May 2025, I took a trip to London, returning to campus in August after the summer holidays. I noticed I was slowly gaining weight; by January this year I’d gained 10lb. I put it down to my late-night snacking and lack of exercise.\n Continue reading...	https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/sep/04/experience-i-didnt-know-i-was-pregnant-until-i-gave-birth	\N	UK	2026-09-04 04:00:57	2026-09-04 18:32:19.914	cmtlwyprl000zhjil34s657op	{"life and style",pregnancy,"parents and parenting",family,"health & wellbeing"}
cmtnajsuj004833itakb85pvr	The best hair dryers for smooth, speedy styling at home – whatever your hair type	Want every day to be a good hair day? We tested 22 hair dryers to find the best, from gentle diffusers to high-speed and travel-ready models\n• The best hot brushes, tried and tested by our expert\nIn my years of reviewing beauty tech, it was upgrading my hair dryer that made the biggest difference to my routine. I used to dread hair-wash days: the chore of shampooing, conditioning and rinsing my hair, plus the time – and aching arms – spent getting it dry again.\nMy clunky, bargain-bucket hair dryer of seven years was weighty, deafeningly loud, and took a painstaking 20 minutes to dry my hair. So happier days really did arrive when I switched to a new model.\n Continue reading...	https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter/2025/aug/26/best-hairdryers-uk	\N	UK	2026-09-04 09:00:24	2026-09-04 18:32:19.915	cmtlwyprl000zhjil34s657op	{"hair care","women's hair","men's hair","life and style",technology,beauty}
cmtnajsuk004933itq3o7qawv	The best backpacks in the UK for work, travel and wild adventure – tested	Whether you want a smart-but-stylish commuter rucksack or a hike-friendly pack, our writer lugged 16 over hundreds of miles to find the best bags for your buck\n• The best travel mugs for taking hot drinks on the go\nChart your course through a fun, active or productive day, and you’ll often find cause to carry things. Backpacks are arguably the best people-powered way to do it, used by pretty much everyone from Napoleonic soldiers and Ötzi the Iceman to ultra-marathoner Courtney Dauwalter, as well as innumerable workers, students and travellers.\nThe best backpack to choose depends on which elements of your own world you wish to carry, and where you’re planning to take them. You can choose between smart-looking options suitable for work and travel, hiking-focused day packs and trail packs designed for outdoor itineraries, and versatile backpacks with water-resistant materials and a high storage capacity.\n Continue reading...	https://www.theguardian.com/thefilter/2026/sep/04/best-backpacks-tested-uk	\N	UK	2026-09-04 14:00:09	2026-09-04 18:32:19.916	cmtlwyprl000zhjil34s657op	{walking,fitness,"life and style",hobbies,"health & wellbeing"}
